not permission to infer new controller, animation, or presentation semantics.

Phase-three physical coordinates are now an intake invariant rather than an
adapter convention. A whole generated-index audit covers 161,960 current
physical members: member paths are unique within every package, and all 132,179
members that carry a source chunk ordinal also have a package-unique ordinal.
Across the 12 package categories with normalized component ledgers, all 132,179
path-bearing ledger rows map one-to-one to those same phase-three members by
exact published path plus source ordinal, with zero missing or ambiguous rows.

`PhaseThreePackageRow` now rejects duplicate physical member paths and duplicate
non-null source ordinals before any conversion adapter can observe the package.
It also exposes one exact path-and-ordinal lookup. Vehicle and world texture
occurrence joins use that shared boundary, while the world shader coordinate map
can rely on intake uniqueness instead of maintaining a second ambiguity guard.
This centralizes physical occurrence identity only; it does not turn source
ordinal into logical shader, texture, controller, or render relationship
authority.

`shar.world-model-props.v11` closes that deferred world provenance gap using
the centralized phase-three coordinate invariant. Terrain-world intake now
builds one classified source-member table for every source-ordinal package
member. Deferred composite quad groups must resolve as `p3d-mesh` model members,
frame-controller-family relationships as `p3d-controller` controller members,
and retained BQG animations as `p3d-animation` animation members at the exact
ledger path and source ordinal.

The catalog now serializes those stable phase-three ids beside the existing
normalized member ids and source ordinals. This covers the previously audited
1,091 quad groups, 2,802 frame-controller-family rows, and 4,032 animations
without changing composite selection, controller-to-animation matching, BQG
validation, or presentation semantics. A classification mismatch fails closed;
phase-three identity still records a physical occurrence rather than inventing
a logical relationship.

The next bounded world provenance gap is the primary model route rather than the
deferred render path. A route-level audit mirrors the current world inventory
across 840 model-bearing terrain-world candidates. It finds 370 rigid-animated
candidates, 55 composite-backed static candidates, and 415 static candidates
without a matching composite. Composite selection retains 2,368 mesh
occurrences in total; every selected mesh resolves to an exact phase-three
`p3d-mesh` model member at its ledger path and source ordinal.

All 425 matching composite occurrences likewise resolve as phase-three
`p3d-composite-drawable` model members. Their authored skeleton relationships
resolve to 425 exact `p3d-skeleton` animation members. Of those candidates, 370
also have the exact same-container `PTRN_<skeleton>` relationship used by the
rigid-animated route, and all 370 clips resolve as `p3d-animation` animation
members. The remaining 55 composites have the authored skeleton but no exact
PTRN clip, so the current route remains static and does not consume that
