The world catalog source alias currently publishes none of those primary
phase-three member ids; it retains only package/container identity plus deferred
render evidence. A future catalog revision can add source-order selected mesh
member ids and separately labelled composite/skeleton/PTRN provenance without
changing semantic deduplication or implying that the 55 static skeletons were
exported. This is a physical-provenance gap only; current mesh selection and
animation routing remain source-backed.

This umbrella task remains open for broader topology, UV, material, texture,
pivot, rig, animation, placement, and transform evidence.
